      "locator": "q49",
      "text": "49. Choose the correct ANTONYM for sullen from the options given below. (1) morose (2) reticent (3) timid (4) genial",
      "url": "https://infinitylearn.com/surge/wp-content/uploads/securepdfs/2025/05/CUET-English-Question-Paper-2024.pdf",
      "publisher": "infinitylearn.com",
      "title": null
    },
    "cuet2024-english-bookA-q49-capture-fec22fec900f:checked-excerpt": {
      "id": "cuet2024-english-bookA-q49-capture-fec22fec900f",
      "locator": "checked-excerpt",
      "text": "in a bad mood and not speaking, either on a particular occasion or because it is part of your character",
      "url": "https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/sullen",
      "publisher": "www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com",
      "title": null
    },
    "cuet2024-english-bookA-q49-capture-23c3cd612dde:checked-excerpt": {
      "id": "cuet2024-english-bookA-q49-capture-23c3cd612dde",
      "locator": "checked-excerpt",
      "text": "friendly and cheerful",
      "url": "https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/us/definition/english/genial",
      "publisher": "www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com",
      "title": null
    },
    "cuet2024-english-bookA-paper:q46": {
      "id": "cuet2024-english-bookA-paper",
      "locator": "q46",
      "text": "46. Identify the option closest in meaning to the underlined word : The movie star’s biography is a glossy, sycophantic portrayal. (1) cowardly (2) domineering (3) flattering (4) insolent",
      "url": "https://infinitylearn.com/surge/wp-content/uploads/securepdfs/2025/05/CUET-English-Question-Paper-2024.pdf",
      "publisher": "infinitylearn.com",
      "title": null
    },
    "cuet2024-english-bookA-q46-capture-2326f94598e9:checked-excerpt": {
      "id": "cuet2024-english-bookA-q46-capture-2326f94598e9",
      "locator": "checked-excerpt",
      "text": "praising important or powerful people too much and in a way that is not sincere, especially in order to get something from them",
      "url": "https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/sycophantic",
      "publisher": "www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com",
      "title": null
    },
    "cuet2024-english-bookA-q46-capture-2fd905f3a9d9:checked-excerpt": {
      "id": "cuet2024-english-bookA-q46-capture-2fd905f3a9d9",
      "locator": "checked-excerpt",
      "text": "to say nice things about somebody, often in a way that is not sincere, because you want them to do something for you or you want to please them",
      "url": "https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/flatter",
      "publisher": "www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com",
      "title": null
    },
    "cuet2024-english-bookA-paper:q48": {
      "id": "cuet2024-english-bookA-paper",
      "locator": "q48",
      "text": "48. Choose the correct SYNONYM for redoubtable from the options given below. (1) flimsy (2) perplexing (3) formidable (4) voluble",
      "url": "https://infinitylearn.com/surge/wp-content/uploads/securepdfs/2025/05/CUET-English-Question-Paper-2024.pdf",
      "publisher": "infinitylearn.com",
      "title": null
    },
    "cuet2024-english-bookA-q48-capture-5b560b67fcda:checked-excerpt": {
      "id": "cuet2024-english-bookA-q48-capture-5b560b67fcda",
      "locator": "checked-excerpt",
      "text": "if a person is redoubtable, they have very strong qualities that make you respect them and perhaps feel afraid of them",
      "url": "https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/redoubtable",
      "publisher": "www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com",
      "title": null
    }
